# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-3), L §2.3 `instant`, §4.6: a balance reading stands at the start or the end of a day;
# the instant `after m` is cut, so a row that writes it is refused by the grammar. A running balance printed row by
# row is stated once a day, `at D end`. (Was L4_6_after_plan_refused, LOAD-ORDER for a reading after a plan.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  anchor konto
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 5
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  stated[konto] = 900.00 PLN after pay[2026-01] "s"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: expected end of line, got after (m.tally:27)
